# Which killed more in the 20th century: smallpox or the World Wars?
subtitle: "Pick the bigger killer, smallpox or the two World Wars, then see the gap drawn to scale, and how a vaccine wiped smallpox out for good."
tags: ["history","medicine","epidemiology"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Which killed more?\" note \"?\""

## Which killed more in the 20th century: smallpox or the World Wars?
affirm: plain
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Both World Wars
      - Smallpox
    values:
      - 95
      - 300
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 320
    y_label: Deaths, millions
    bar_colors: each
    label_size: 30
    icons:
      - {of: crossed swords, set: twemoji}
      - {of: microbe, set: twemoji}
    box:
      x: 60
      'y': 370
      w: 880
      h: 300
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Smallpox
      authors: Sophie Ochmann, Saloni Dattani and Max Roser (Our World in Data)
      year: 2018
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/smallpox
      finding: an estimated 300 million people died of smallpox in the 20th century (D. A. Henderson); about 30% of people infected with variola major died; vaccine developed in 1796; last case October 1977 in Merka, Somalia; eradication certified May 1980, the first-ever eradication of a human disease; the Intensified Eradication Programme cost about $300 million, 1967–1977
    - id: henderson
      title: The eradication of smallpox — An overview of the past, present, and future
      authors: D. A. Henderson
      year: 2011
      doi: 10.1016/j.vaccine.2011.06.080
      finding: an estimated 300 million people died of smallpox in the 20th century
    - id: ww1
      title: World War I casualties
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2025
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_I_casualties
      finding: about 15 to 22 million military and civilian deaths
    - id: ww2
      title: World War II casualties
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2025
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II_casualties
      finding: about 70 to 85 million deaths, military and civilian

    cards duel cites ["owid","ww1","ww2"] size 2 y 470 compare "Which killed more (millions)?" hidden true
        * "Both World Wars" icon.of "crossed swords" icon.set twemoji value 95
        * "Smallpox, 1900s" icon.of microbe icon.set twemoji value 300
    path c1 dashed thick #8f887c points [[-0.45,95],[1.38,95]] data true hidden true
    path c2 dashed thick #8f887c points [[0.62,190],[1.38,190]] data true hidden true
    text x3 "×3" right bar_2 gap 40 #8a5fa8 font_size 64 hidden true
    path tl_line thick #3d3833 points [[70,220],[930,220]] hidden true
    shape tl_d1 #3d3833 shape circle x 140 y 220 radius 9 style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    text tl_y1 "1796" #3d3833 cites ["owid"] x 140 y 258 font_size 40 hidden true
    text tl_w1 "vaccine" #3d3833 x 140 y 180 font_size 38 hidden true
    shape tl_d2 #3d3833 shape circle x 420 y 220 radius 9 style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    text tl_y2 "1967" #3d3833 cites ["owid"] x 420 y 258 font_size 40 hidden true
    text tl_w2 "final push" #3d3833 x 420 y 180 font_size 38 hidden true
    shape tl_d3 #3d3833 shape circle x 660 y 220 radius 9 style.fill #3d3833 hidden true
    text tl_y3 "1977" #3d3833 cites ["owid"] x 660 y 258 font_size 40 hidden true
    text tl_w3 "last case" #3d3833 x 660 y 180 font_size 38 hidden true
    shape tl_d4 #2f6b8f shape circle x 870 y 220 radius 9 style.fill #2f6b8f hidden true
    text tl_y4 "1980" #2f6b8f cites ["owid"] x 870 y 258 font_size 40 hidden true
    text tl_w4 "gone" #2f6b8f x 870 y 180 font_size 38 hidden true

    card title "Smallpox or the World Wars?"

A: Here's one: which killed more people in the twentieth century, both World Wars together, or one disease, smallpox?
    draw duel

B: Smells like a trick question. I'll go with the disease.
    highlight duel_2

    ask "Tap the bigger killer." on duel store g reveal.text Smallpox! reveal.at.x 700 reveal.at.y 615 reveal.size 56
        right: Smallpox, by far: about three hundred million deaths in that century alone.

    erase duel

A: You were right. The two World Wars together killed around ninety-five million people, soldiers and civilians.
    draw axes bar_1

A: Smallpox, in the same hundred years: about three hundred million, mostly children.
    draw bar_2

B: So stack both wars three times, and you still don't reach it.
    draw c1 c2 x3

B: Then why has nobody I know ever had it?
    group tl members ["tl_line","tl_d1","tl_y1","tl_w1","tl_d2","tl_y2","tl_w2","tl_d3","tl_y3","tl_w3","tl_d4","tl_y4","tl_w4"]

A: Because it's gone. A vaccine existed from 1796, but the final worldwide push only began in 1967. The last natural case was in Somalia in 1977.
    highlight tl

A: In 1980 smallpox was declared eradicated: the first human disease ever wiped out. That last ten-year campaign cost about three hundred million dollars.
    highlight bar_2

B: Three hundred million dollars, against three hundred million deaths. About a dollar a life.
    highlight bar_2

A: The vaccine was old news. What finished smallpox was getting it to everyone, village by village.
    highlight tl

